WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.129 --> 00:00:01.320
(crowd applauding)
- All right, let's finish up

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.700
with a story I hope will get you

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.320
into the early spirit of the season.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.656
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.656 --> 00:00:08.430
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.580
Tomorrow morning marks the
unofficial start of the holidays.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.413
I'm talking about

00:00:12.413 --> 00:00:15.780
the 97th Macy's Thanksgiving
Day Parade, people.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.720
And they are delivering more
parade coverage than ever

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.836
with a three and a half hour event.

00:00:20.836 --> 00:00:23.190
There are new floats and balloons,

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.800
performances from some of
Broadway's biggest shows,

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.480
and of course, old
Saint Nick will be there

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.330
to close out the festivities
like he always does.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.060
Here with a sneak peek,
let's everybody say hello

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.760
to the executive producer
of the parade, Will Coss.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.729
What's up Will?
(audience applauding)

00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:40.514
- Hi, how's it going? How are you?

00:00:40.514 --> 00:00:41.504
- I'm good, man.

00:00:41.504 --> 00:00:42.337
Thank you for joining us.

00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:43.910
How is planning going?

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.300
- Planning is great.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.660
We've had a very busy last 12 months

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.190
building our brand new floats, balloons,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.470
getting all the parade
elements ready to go,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.470
finalizing our marching
bands, our performance groups.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.240
It's set to be a pretty exciting show

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.680
on Thanksgiving morning.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.330
- It must be crazy, it's a moving show.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:03.133
I've been a part of it, but I
would never want to run that.

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:05.422
It's a lot of moving parts, man.

00:01:05.422 --> 00:01:08.040
So volunteers are key for you, right?

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:09.180
- Volunteers are key.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.422
The parade actually started 1924

00:01:11.422 --> 00:01:14.070
with volunteers from
Macy's, and we've continued

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.080
that tradition over the last 97 parades.

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.430
So we'll have over
5,000 volunteers join us

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.170
and up to 8,000 people,

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.030
including all of our
performance groups, our bands.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:26.640
So it's a big day, it's
a lot of folks coming.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.550
A lot of folks excited to
bring the holiday tradition

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.105
back to the streets of New York City.

00:01:31.105 --> 00:01:32.599
- Absolutely.

00:01:32.599 --> 00:01:35.880
Well everybody, the 97th
Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.770
kicks off at 8:30 Eastern,

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:40.290
airing on NBC and streaming on Peacock.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.790
Thank you so much, Will.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:42.798
I'm liking your post right now, man.

00:01:42.798 --> 00:01:43.631
- Thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:01:43.631 --> 00:01:46.131
- Good luck.
- Happy Thanksgiving everyone.

00:01:46.131 --> 00:01:47.113
(crowd continues cheering)

00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:50.130
- All right, so usually at this point

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.110
we give our guest $1,000 courtesy of

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.540
our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.610
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:58.740
But we are kicking off the
holiday season right here

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.270
by giving it to someone in the audience.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.561
So,
(audience cheering)

00:02:01.561 --> 00:02:05.673
pay attention to this monitor

00:02:05.673 --> 00:02:09.023
and one of your faces is gonna show up.

00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:14.023
(drum roll)
(audience cheering)

00:02:15.262 --> 00:02:17.798
(upbeat music)
(crowd clapping)

00:02:17.798 --> 00:02:20.715
(symbols crashing)

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.553
Yes! What's your name?

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.718
- Hi, my name is Logan Smith.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.050
- Oh my gosh, nice to meet you.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:35.400
What are you gonna do with the money?

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.530
- I have no idea.
(audience laughing)

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.390
- Well you gotta have a
little bit of fun with it.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.040
People always say bills, that's nice.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.210
That's nice, pay some bills.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:44.247
But have some fun with it. Do you promise?

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.080
Just a little bit.
- Oh yeah,

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:46.140
I'm in my traveling era right now.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.322
- Oh, yes.

00:02:47.322 --> 00:02:50.086
(crowd clapping)
Go somewhere fantastic.

00:02:50.086 --> 00:02:52.272
I love this for you. Enjoy it!

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:53.570
Thank you for coming to the show

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.654
and thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:55.654 --> 00:02:59.730
Taika Waititi, John
O'Hurley, Jason Reynolds,

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.158
Natalie Pasquarella, John Gizza,

00:03:02.158 --> 00:03:04.996
the high-tech High Choir, and our friends

00:03:04.996 --> 00:03:08.058
at NBC4 New York-
(crowd drowns out monologue).

00:03:08.058 --> 00:03:09.012
Have a great day.

00:03:09.012 --> 00:03:10.762
And if it's not, try and change it.

